<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles (Homo sapiens (human retinal arterial and microvascular bifurcation network))",
        "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens (human retinal arterial and microvascular bifurcation network) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Homo sapiens (human retinal arterial and microvascular bifurcation network) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-vascular-cube-law-branching-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py> ;
    schema:about "Homo sapiens (human retinal arterial and microvascular bifurcation network)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Independent human morphometric confirmation of the F-L exponent shift, of the AVR (an input), or of arteriovenous interdigitation (index 0.504 ~ random mixing, reference 1.0 is an idealisation); verification of the three Pass 3 DOIs (recalled offline, flagged in bib, JSON and script header)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fahraeus-Lindqvist eta(r) in the Poiseuille term, generalised stationarity 2 P_met = (4 - eps) P_visc, local gamma_eff(r), symmetric junction exponent gamma_j(r_0) and a Newtonian-vs-F-L tree exponent sweep (gamma* 3.000 -> 2.773)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Geodesic arterial and venous Murray trees on a 12 mm sphere with tangent-plane Murray angles, AVR-coupled venous root, repulsive A/V coupling with an uncoupled control, orthographic fundus-projection foreshortening and projected A/V crossings",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Green-channel top-hat / Zhang-Suen skeleton / EDT segmentation of the vendored human fundus specimen (N = 19 Y-junctions)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Power functional, stationarity radius, wall shear invariance, asymmetric cosine laws, Zamir/Steiner/Da Vinci ablation controls, 7-generation Sherman hierarchy and the gamma power sweep (Newtonian)",
        "reported_in_source: Fåhraeus & Lindqvist (1931) / Pries et al. (1992): the apparent viscosity of blood falls in tubes narrower than ~300 um, fitted by eta_rel(D) = 220 e^{-1.3D} + 3.2 - 2.44 e^{-0.06 D^0.645} at H_D = 0.45",
        "reported_in_source: Hubbard et al. (1999): the clinical retinal arteriole-to-venule caliber ratio is about 2/3",
        "reported_in_source: Murray (1926a): minimising Poiseuille pumping power plus a metabolic cost proportional to blood volume gives Q proportional to r^3 and a scale-invariant wall shear stress sqrt(eta b); at the optimum the metabolic term is twice the viscous term",
        "reported_in_source: Murray (1926b): the same functional fixes the bifurcation angles via cos(theta_1) = (r_0^4 + r_1^4 - r_2^4)/(2 r_0^2 r_1^2) and its mirror; symmetric total angle 74.93 deg",
        "reported_in_source: Zamir (1976): alternative optimality principles (surface, volume, drag, power) give different angle laws; Sherman (1981): the cube law holds across generations of a tree",
        "transfer_boundary: The 3D retinal cup is a reduced geometric model: no haemodynamic network solve, no capillary bed connecting arterial and venous tips, no oxygen/VEGF-guided angiogenesis, optic disc at the posterior pole; the venous root radius is an input (AVR = 0.67), not emergent",
        "transfer_boundary: The F-L fit is the in-vitro glass-tube relation at fixed H_D = 0.45 (no in-vivo endothelial surface layer correction, no phase separation at bifurcations), applied per generation to a symmetric tree; the '~2.7' target is reached by the tree optimum (2.773) but not by the local junction exponent (2.859 at 25 um)",
        "transfer_boundary: The J01-J08 'Zamir 1979' junction table carries a Murray-prediction column and agrees with Murray to <= 0.3 deg without page/figure provenance, so the RMSE = 0.134 deg / r = 0.9999 figures are a parity check, not independent validation; the Sherman (1981) hierarchy table is generated from r_g = 82 um * 2^(-g/3), not digitised" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "6. Tip-Splitting & Flow Trees" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Bifurcating Vascular/Lung Trees" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Murray Law r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Homo" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py; output: docs/media/vascular_cube_law_branching_comparison.png; organism: Homo sapiens (human retinal arterial and microvascular bifurcation network); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 04d15104fa016f1fef6000d63f1ce9e4b79872913b2d27ac2256b74bf7018717; artifact_sha256: becaebe2165f42d7be388e4b462b950552999bac5c8fcf6170dcc8cf2541775a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/fahraeus_lindqvist_retinal_cup_reference.json=f9c04d6dabecbe31..., datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/retinal_vasculature_specimen.jpg=bc548d4150e070a5..., datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json=6d1761f2e01e4fa7...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-vascular-cube-law-branching-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Murray (1926a): minimising Poiseuille pumping power plus a metabolic cost proportional to blood volume gives Q proportional to r^3 and a scale-invariant wall shear stress sqrt(eta b); at the optimum the metabolic term is twice the viscous term | Murray (1926b): the same functional fixes the bifurcation angles via cos(theta_1) = (r_0^4 + r_1^4 - r_2^4)/(2 r_0^2 r_1^2) and its mirror; symmetric total angle 74.93 deg | Zamir (1976): alternative optimality principles (surface, volume, drag, power) give different angle laws; Sherman (1981): the cube law holds across generations of a tree | Fåhraeus & Lindqvist (1931) / Pries et al. (1992): the apparent viscosity of blood falls in tubes narrower than ~300 um, fitted by eta_rel(D) = 220 e^{-1.3D} + 3.2 - 2.44 e^{-0.06 D^0.645} at H_D = 0.45 | Hubbard et al. (1999): the clinical retinal arteriole-to-venule caliber ratio is about 2/3; reconstructed_in_script: Power functional, stationarity radius, wall shear invariance, asymmetric cosine laws, Zamir/Steiner/Da Vinci ablation controls, 7-generation Sherman hierarchy and the gamma power sweep (Newtonian) | Fahraeus-Lindqvist eta(r) in the Poiseuille term, generalised stationarity 2 P_met = (4 - eps) P_visc, local gamma_eff(r), symmetric junction exponent gamma_j(r_0) and a Newtonian-vs-F-L tree exponent sweep (gamma* 3.000 -> 2.773) | Geodesic arterial and venous Murray trees on a 12 mm sphere with tangent-plane Murray angles, AVR-coupled venous root, repulsive A/V coupling with an uncoupled control, orthographic fundus-projection foreshortening and projected A/V crossings | Green-channel top-hat / Zhang-Suen skeleton / EDT segmentation of the vendored human fundus specimen (N = 19 Y-junctions); transfer_boundary: The 3D retinal cup is a reduced geometric model: no haemodynamic network solve, no capillary bed connecting arterial and venous tips, no oxygen/VEGF-guided angiogenesis, optic disc at the posterior pole; the venous root radius is an input (AVR = 0.67), not emergent | The F-L fit is the in-vitro glass-tube relation at fixed H_D = 0.45 (no in-vivo endothelial surface layer correction, no phase separation at bifurcations), applied per generation to a symmetric tree; the '~2.7' target is reached by the tree optimum (2.773) but not by the local junction exponent (2.859 at 25 um) | The J01-J08 'Zamir 1979' junction table carries a Murray-prediction column and agrees with Murray to <= 0.3 deg without page/figure provenance, so the RMSE = 0.134 deg / r = 0.9999 figures are a parity check, not independent validation; the Sherman (1981) hierarchy table is generated from r_g = 82 um * 2^(-g/3), not digitised; does_not_claim: Independent human morphometric confirmation of the F-L exponent shift, of the AVR (an input), or of arteriovenous interdigitation (index 0.504 ~ random mixing, reference 1.0 is an idealisation); verification of the three Pass 3 DOIs (recalled offline, flagged in bib, JSON and script header)]" ;
    pk1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(76)90058-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0161-6420(99)90525-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1085/jgp.78.4.431>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1085/jgp.9.6.835>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpheart.1992.263.6.H1770>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1152/ajplegacy.1931.96.3.562> ;
    pk1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity>,
