<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles — Code-to-model traceability: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header (L1-22) maps the Pass 3 additions to Sections 4b/4c, the three new sources and Lean Laws 4-5; every F-L function cites Pries (1992) Eq. 1 and states the normalisation; the cup section states its reduced-model boundary; the math KG loop file registers all five laws with Lean theorem names and refreshed code loci (L22-113, Law 4 L77-97, Law 5 L98-113) and new `model_spec` keys; measurement entries name the Lean theorem they rest on (L1605-1614, L1636-1645). Deductions: the `--self-test` help string and the `self_test()` docstring still say \"Pass 2\" (L1670, L1779) (-2); the handedness rule for A/V coupling (L714-727) and the 95 deg polar limit / 4 deg disc radius constants (L644-646) have no source beyond a comment (-3); the 82 um root radius attribution to Sherman (1981) is unsourced (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py L1779–L1779: --self-test help text still reads 'Pass 2 self-test suite' after the Pass 3 extension <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py#L1779-L1779>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles — Model fidelity to source: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Murray's (1926a) power functional, stationarity radius and exact tau_w = sqrt(eta b) invariance (L121-166, L305-359), Murray's (1926b) asymmetric cosine laws with Zamir, Steiner and Da Vinci controls (L175-240, L361-443) are unchanged and correct. Pass 3 adds the Fahraeus-Lindqvist mechanism correctly: eta(r) normalised so the large-vessel limit equals Murray's eta (L467-483), generalised stationarity Q*(r) = (pi/2) r^3 sqrt(b/(eta(r)(4 - eps))) with eps = d ln eta / d ln r (L486-521) and a bisection junction exponent (L524-551); the 3D cup uses exact geodesic stepping and Rodrigues tangent-plane rotations with cube-law radii (L655-745) and a flow-balance venous coupling k_v/k_a = sum r^3 / sum R^3 (L761-890). Five machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 `sorry`s). Deductions: the retinal cup is a kinematic growth rule with no haemodynamic solve or capillary closure, and its A/V \"coupling\" is a heuristic handedness choice (L714-727) that segregates territories rather than producing paired arcades (-4); the F-L fit is in-vitro at fixed H_D = 0.45 with no phase separation, and eta(r) is applied generation-wise to a symmetric tree (-2); the empirical junction evaluator (L242-300) still scores a table that is itself Murray-generated (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py L714–L727: A/V coupling is a geometric handedness rule (keep the side farther from the nearest rival node); no haemodynamic or angiogenic mechanism <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py#L714-L727>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1497-1666) now reports 15 metrics with reference values, methods, dispersion statistics and ablation controls; the 7 new entries include a parity check of the implemented F-L fit (eta_rel(10 um) = 1.328 vs 1.33), the tree optimum gamma*_FL = 2.773 with Newtonian control 3.000, the junction exponent 2.859 at 25 um, the sphericity residual 7e-15 mm, the AVR propagation with derived venous shear/b_v, the interdigitation index with uncoupled control, and the projection bias by eccentricity. Deductions: the headline Pass 2 claims (RMSE 0.134 deg, r = 0.9999 for J01-J08, L1545-1554) rest on a table that contains its own Murray prediction and has no page/figure provenance, so they are circular rather than validating (-6); the F-L reference value 2.7 (L1605-1614) is the Pass 2 audit's target, not a literature datum, and the stated reference_source says so (-3); the AVR metric (L1636-1645) equals its reference by construction (-2); the interdigitation reference 1.0 (L1646-1655) is an idealisation and the result 0.504 shows the coupling fails its purpose (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py L1605–L1614: gamma*_FL reference_value 2.7 is the Pass 2 audit remediation target, not a literature datum <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py#L1605-L1614>",
        "1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py L1636–L1655: AVR = 0.67 is an input (--avr) so value == reference by construction; interdigitation reference 1.0 is an idealisation, measured 0.504 ~ random <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py#L1636-L1655>",
        "datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json L81–L90: J01-J08 rows carry murray_predicted_total_deg and agree with it to <= 0.3 deg; no page/figure provenance — the RMSE/r metrics are circular <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json#L81-L90>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-3d-retinal-cup-geodesic-tree-sphericity-residual-max-p-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-arteriovenous-interdigitation-index-of-terminal-tips-on-the-retinal-cup-repulsive-coupling>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-coupled-arteriovenous-root-caliber-ratio-avr-artery-vein-on-the-retinal-cup>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-da-vinci-area-preserving-control-gamma-2-excess-vascular-tree-power-penalty>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-empirical-human-retinal-bifurcation-angle-rmse-murray-prediction-vs-j01-j08>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-empirical-retinal-cube-law-conservation-ratio-r-1-3-r-2-3-1-3-r-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-fahraeus-lindqvist-power-minimising-tree-exponent-gamma-fl-7-generation-sweep>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-fahraeus-lindqvist-relative-apparent-viscosity-eta-rel-at-d-10-um-h-d-0-45>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-fahraeus-lindqvist-symmetric-junction-exponent-gamma-j-at-pre-capillary-r-0-25-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-fundus-projection-foreshortening-bias-of-bifurcation-angle-theta-proj-theta-true-peripheral-60-deg-eccentricity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-generational-wall-shear-stress-tau-w-across-7-sherman-1981-arteriole-levels>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-metabolic-to-viscous-power-ratio-at-optimal-radius-p-met-r-p-visc-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-measurement-segmented-retinal-fundus-specimen-y-junction-bifurcation-angle-mean>,
