<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles — MorphoEval overall 89.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3 remediated) evaluation of `1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py` (89.2/100, down 1.7 from 90.9/100 in Pass 2). Both Pass 2 remediation items landed: Section 4b implements Pries et al. (1992) Fahraeus-Lindqvist apparent viscosity in the Poiseuille term with the generalised stationarity 2 P_met = (4 - eps) P_visc (Lean 4 `fahraeus_lindqvist_stationarity_shift`), shifting the 7-generation power-minimising exponent from 3.000 to 2.773 (junction exponent at 25 um 2.859); Section 4c grows coupled arterial and venous Murray trees by exact geodesic steps on a 12 mm hemispherical retinal cup (sphericity residual 7e-15 mm) with AVR-coupled venous root (Lean 4 `arteriovenous_coupled_cube_balance`), a repulsive A/V coupling versus an uncoupled control, fundus-projection foreshortening (3.3 deg central, 32.4 deg peripheral) and a new 3D GIF. The figure now has 9 panels, `measure_morphoeval()` 15 entries and `self_test()` 9 suites (all pass, 2.6 s; render 4.9 s). The score nonetheless falls because the round exposed defects v2 had credited: the J01-J08 junction table is prescribed/circular and its source (Zamir, Medeiros & Cunningham 1979) is uncited in the bib, the Sherman hierarchy table is synthetic, three new DOIs are unverified, the F-L \"2.7\" reference is the audit's own target, the interdigitation item is only partially closed (index 0.504 vs 0.41 control, random level), and the specimen measurement still uses an uncorrected planar reference angle. Overall 89.2/100 (faithfulness 88.2, reproducibility 91.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/vascular_cube_law_branching_comparison.png: rendered output of 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py at 028758bc, image/png, 1139022 B, 2520×2184 px, artifact_sha256 becaebe2165f42d7be388e4b462b950552999bac5c8fcf6170dcc8cf2541775a (sha256 becaebe2165f42d7be388e4b462b950552999bac5c8fcf6170dcc8cf2541775a), spec_fingerprint 04d15104fa016f1fef6000d63f1ce9e4b79872913b2d27ac2256b74bf7018717. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 04d15104fa016f1fef6000d63f1ce9e4b79872913b2d27ac2256b74bf7018717; artifact_sha256: becaebe2165f42d7be388e4b462b950552999bac5c8fcf6170dcc8cf2541775a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/fahraeus_lindqvist_retinal_cup_reference.json=f9c04d6dabecbe31..., datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/retinal_vasculature_specimen.jpg=bc548d4150e070a5..., datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json=6d1761f2e01e4fa7...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-vascular-cube-law-branching-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Murray (1926a): minimising Poiseuille pumping power plus a metabolic cost proportional to blood volume gives Q proportional to r^3 and a scale-invariant wall shear stress sqrt(eta b); at the optimum the metabolic term is twice the viscous term | Murray (1926b): the same functional fixes the bifurcation angles via cos(theta_1) = (r_0^4 + r_1^4 - r_2^4)/(2 r_0^2 r_1^2) and its mirror; symmetric total angle 74.93 deg | Zamir (1976): alternative optimality principles (surface, volume, drag, power) give different angle laws; Sherman (1981): the cube law holds across generations of a tree | Fåhraeus & Lindqvist (1931) / Pries et al. (1992): the apparent viscosity of blood falls in tubes narrower than ~300 um, fitted by eta_rel(D) = 220 e^{-1.3D} + 3.2 - 2.44 e^{-0.06 D^0.645} at H_D = 0.45 | Hubbard et al. (1999): the clinical retinal arteriole-to-venule caliber ratio is about 2/3; reconstructed_in_script: Power functional, stationarity radius, wall shear invariance, asymmetric cosine laws, Zamir/Steiner/Da Vinci ablation controls, 7-generation Sherman hierarchy and the gamma power sweep (Newtonian) | Fahraeus-Lindqvist eta(r) in the Poiseuille term, generalised stationarity 2 P_met = (4 - eps) P_visc, local gamma_eff(r), symmetric junction exponent gamma_j(r_0) and a Newtonian-vs-F-L tree exponent sweep (gamma* 3.000 -> 2.773) | Geodesic arterial and venous Murray trees on a 12 mm sphere with tangent-plane Murray angles, AVR-coupled venous root, repulsive A/V coupling with an uncoupled control, orthographic fundus-projection foreshortening and projected A/V crossings | Green-channel top-hat / Zhang-Suen skeleton / EDT segmentation of the vendored human fundus specimen (N = 19 Y-junctions); transfer_boundary: The 3D retinal cup is a reduced geometric model: no haemodynamic network solve, no capillary bed connecting arterial and venous tips, no oxygen/VEGF-guided angiogenesis, optic disc at the posterior pole; the venous root radius is an input (AVR = 0.67), not emergent | The F-L fit is the in-vitro glass-tube relation at fixed H_D = 0.45 (no in-vivo endothelial surface layer correction, no phase separation at bifurcations), applied per generation to a symmetric tree; the '~2.7' target is reached by the tree optimum (2.773) but not by the local junction exponent (2.859 at 25 um) | The J01-J08 'Zamir 1979' junction table carries a Murray-prediction column and agrees with Murray to <= 0.3 deg without page/figure provenance, so the RMSE = 0.134 deg / r = 0.9999 figures are a parity check, not independent validation; the Sherman (1981) hierarchy table is generated from r_g = 82 um * 2^(-g/3), not digitised; does_not_claim: Independent human morphometric confirmation of the F-L exponent shift, of the AVR (an input), or of arteriovenous interdigitation (index 0.504 ~ random mixing, reference 1.0 is an idealisation); verification of the three Pass 3 DOIs (recalled offline, flagged in bib, JSON and script header)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py:1064 and 1575-1584 with 1656-1665 — the specimen Y-junction reference 74.93 deg is a tangent-plane quantity while the segmented angles are planar projections; apply the computed eccentricity-dependent foreshortening correction to the specimen junctions (or compare against the projected Murray angle) and remove the hard-coded tortuosity fallback 1.01.",
        "remediation needed: 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py:1605-1614 — gamma*_FL reference_value 2.7 is the Pass 2 audit's own target. Cite a literature value for the F-L-modified Murray exponent (e.g. Alarcón, Byrne & Maini 2005 Microvasc. Res. 69:156, DOI to be verified) and report both the tree optimum (2.773) and the junction exponent (2.859) against it.",
        "remediation needed: 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py:1670 and 1779 — the self_test() docstring and the --self-test help string still read \"Pass 2\"; update to the 9-suite Pass 3 description.",
        "remediation needed: 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py:1787, 1104, 1812 and 1113 — `--seed` is accepted but unused in every default path, and `--eta`/`--b` still do not reach run_gamma_power_sweep / Panel D / the empirical junction evaluator. Either consume the seed (e.g. heading jitter in the cup) or drop the flag; thread eta/b through the Newtonian sweep.",
        "remediation needed: 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py:714-727 and 1646-1655 — the repulsive A/V handedness rule yields an interdigitation index of 0.504 (uncoupled 0.41), i.e. random mixing; the Pass 2 item \"coupled arteriovenous interdigitation\" is only partially closed. Implement a venous tree grown toward arterial terminal territories (e.g. tip-attraction to arterial tips with a capillary closure) and replace the idealised reference 1.0 with a fundus-derived A/V alternation datum.",
        "remediation needed: 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py:78-80 and datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/ fahraeus_lindqvist_retinal_cup_reference.json — hash-pin both reference JSONs in EXPECTED_SHA256 and verify them fail-closed; verify the three Pass 3 DOIs (Pries 1992, Fåhraeus & Lindqvist 1931, Hubbard 1999) and add a Zamir, Medeiros & Cunningham (1979) bib entry with DOI.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json:72-80 and 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py:84 — the Sherman (1981) generational hierarchy is generated from r_g = 82 um * 2^(-g/3) and the 82 um root radius has no page pin; digitise Sherman's Table I (or another page-pinned human retinal hierarchy) and compare the synthetic hierarchy against it.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json:81-90 with 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py:242-300 and 1545-1554 — the J01-J08 \"Zamir 1979\" table is prescribed/circular (carries murray_predicted_total_deg, agrees to <= 0.3 deg, no page/figure, Zamir, Medeiros & Cunningham 1979 absent from paper_citations.bib). Replace with page-pinned digitised junctions (or the N = 19 segmented specimen junctions) and relabel the RMSE/r metrics as a parity check until then." ;
