<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles — Morphological realism / specimen match: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-locked human retinal fundus specimen is still segmented by green-channel top-hat enhancement, Zhang-Suen thinning and EDT caliber mapping (L896-1086), giving N = 19 Y-junctions (mean 79.28 deg) shown with skeleton/EDT overlays in Panel E (L1261-1293) and the angle histogram in Panel F (L1294-1323); Panel H and the new 3D GIF (L1351-1376, L1418-1444) render an eye-shaped vascular cup with four arterial and four venous arcades, which is a qualitatively closer match to a fundus than the 2D tree. Deductions: the specimen pipeline is byte-for-byte unchanged from Pass 2 and the 3D cup is never compared against the specimen beyond the projection-bias argument (-5); the specimen measurement keeps 74.93 deg as its reference although Pass 3 itself quantifies a 3.3-32.4 deg orthographic foreshortening bias (L1656-1665) and applies no correction (-4); the tortuosity fallback is a hard-coded 1.01 when no branches are found (L1064) (-2); the rendered cup has its optic disc at the posterior pole with no fovea/disc offset and uniformly alternating arcades that look more regular than any real fundus (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py L1064–L1064: tortuosity_mean falls back to a hard-coded 1.01 when no branches are traced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py#L1064-L1064>",
        "1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py L1656–L1665: Projection foreshortening quantified (central 3.3 deg, peripheral 32.4 deg) but the specimen angle measurement is not projection-corrected <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py#L1656-L1665>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

